+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Voyage 1: TodoMVC Vanilla JS
+
+**Stack:** Vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors. localStorage for persistence. Hash-based routing.
+
+**Assets referenced:** `assets/app-template.index.html` (base markup), `assets/app-spec.md` (TodoMVC behaviour spec).
+
+**Implementation shape:**
+- `index.html` derived from the template markup, cleaned of sample list items and comments.
+- `js/app.js` as the single production file. All logic in one file: model layer (todo array, localStorage read/write), DOM rendering, event handling, routing via `hashchange`.
+- `css/app.css` for any overrides beyond the vendored todomvc-common and todomvc-app-css.
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanillajs`. Each item stores `id`, `title`, `completed`.
+
+**Watchbill order:** W1 (add) -> W2 (complete/toggle/clear) -> W3 (edit) -> W4 (display/counter/visibility) -> W5 (routing/filter) -> W6 (persistence). W6 runs last because persistence tests reload the page, so core behaviour must be solid first.
+
+**Note:** This is a greenfield first voyage. No RIGGING.md exists yet; fitting out is owed at harbour after the first working commit.
diff --git a/specs/adding-todos.feature b/specs/adding-todos.feature
