@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user managing my tasks
+  I want to edit an existing todo's title
+  So that I can correct or update what needs to be done
+
+  Rule: Double-clicking a todo label enters editing mode
+
+    Scenario: Double-clicking a todo activates editing mode
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the "Buy milk" todo label
+      Then the "Buy milk" todo is in editing mode
+      And the edit input contains "Buy milk"
+      And the edit input has focus
+
+  Rule: Editing is saved on blur or Enter
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edited title
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" is being edited
+      When the user changes the edit input to "Buy oat milk" and presses Enter
+      Then the todo is titled "Buy oat milk"
+      And the todo is not in editing mode
+
+    Scenario: Blurring the input saves the edited title
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" is being edited
+      When the user changes the edit input to "Buy oat milk" and blurs the input
+      Then the todo is titled "Buy oat milk"
+      And the todo is not in editing mode
+
+  Rule: Empty edited titles remove the todo
+
+    Scenario: Clearing the title and pressing Enter removes the todo
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the "Buy milk" todo label
+      And the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+      Then the "Buy milk" todo is removed
+
+    Scenario: Clearing the title and blurring removes the todo
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the "Buy milk" todo label
+      And the user clears the edit input and blurs the input
+      Then the "Buy milk" todo is removed
+
+  Rule: Escape discards the edit
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Escape reverts the edit
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the "Buy milk" todo label
+      And the user changes the edit input to "Buy oat milk" and presses Escape
+      Then the todo is titled "Buy milk"
+      And the todo is not in editing mode
+
+    Scenario: Editing is trimmed before saving
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the "Buy milk" todo label
+      And the user changes the edit input to "  Buy oat milk  " and presses Enter
+      Then the todo is titled "Buy oat milk"
diff --git a/specs/persistence.feature b/specs/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e42aae1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+Feature: LocalStorage persistence
+  As a user managing my tasks
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my work
+
+  Rule: Todos survive a page reload
+
+    Scenario: Added todos are visible after reload
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists as active
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then a todo titled "Buy milk" exists as active
+
+    Scenario: Completed state persists after reload
+      Given a completed todo titled "Buy milk" exists
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then a completed todo titled "Buy milk" exists
+
+    Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" is being edited
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the "Buy milk" todo is not in editing mode
+
+    Scenario: Deleted todos do not reappear after reload
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists as active
+      When the user clicks the destroy button on the "Buy milk" todo
+      And the page is reloaded
+      Then the app has no todos
