@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+Feature: Routing and filtering
+  As a user managing my tasks
+  I want to filter my todo list by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Rule: Hash-based routes filter the visible todos
+
+    Scenario: All route shows all todos
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists as active
+      And a completed todo titled "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the "Buy milk" todo is visible
+      And the "Buy eggs" todo is visible
+      And the "All" filter is selected
+
+    Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists as active
+      And a completed todo titled "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the "Buy milk" todo is visible
+      And the "Buy eggs" todo is not visible
+      And the "Active" filter is selected
+
+    Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists as active
+      And a completed todo titled "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the "Buy milk" todo is not visible
+      And the "Buy eggs" todo is visible
+      And the "Completed" filter is selected
+
+  Rule: Completing a todo while filtered updates visibility
+
+    Scenario: Completing a todo on the Active filter hides it
+      Given the user navigates to "#/active"
+      And a todo titled "Buy milk" exists as active
+      When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on the "Buy milk" todo
+      Then the "Buy milk" todo is not visible
+
+    Scenario: Default route is All on fresh load
+      Given the app has no todos
+      Then the "All" filter is selected
